#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Listen for the wake word and carry out spoken commands.

openWakeWord listens for the wake word, Parakeet (through sherpa-onnx) turns
the command into text, everyday commands are matched straight away, and Piper
speaks the reply through the TV, all on the Pi. Anything else goes to GPT-6 Luna
through OpenRouter, or to a small local model in llama-server
(cannvas-llm.service) when there's no OpenRouter key or no internet. Audio only
lives in a short memory buffer until the utterance has been checked, and
never leaves the Pi. Only the text of a request the everyday matcher misses does.

It runs as a user service beside the kiosk because it needs the desktop's
PipeWire session for the USB microphone and the TV's speakers. The kiosk page
follows along through /events (server-sent events) on a loopback port, which
cannvas-server proxies as /api/voice/events.
"""

